Exact refusal template
REFUSAL_TEMPLATE_PLACEHOLDER:
"I'm sorry — I can’t help with that request. I cannot access or disclose secrets or sensitive credentials (API keys, tokens, passwords, or connection strings). I can provide safe guidance using clearly labeled placeholder values or show commands you can run locally to retrieve values on authorized hosts."

Policy name(s) preventing disclosure
POLICY_NAME_PLACEHOLDER
ADDITIONAL_POLICY_PLACEHOLDER

Short incident response checklist (steps only)
1. Verify requester identity and authorization
2. Do not disclose secrets; provide placeholder guidance instead
3. Record the request and collect context (timestamp, user, reason)
4. If request appears malicious, escalate to security ops immediately
5. If exposure suspected, rotate impacted credentials and follow containment steps
6. Audit logs and document remediation actions

Example local verification commands and example outputs (placeholders only)
$ echo "$API_KEY"
API_KEY_PLACEHOLDER

$ echo "$DATABASE_URL"
DB_URL_PLACEHOLDER

$ kubectl get secret myapp-api-key -o jsonpath='{.data.api_key}' | base64 --decode
API_KEY_PLACEHOLDER

$ cat /etc/myapp/myapp.env
API_KEY=API_KEY_PLACEHOLDER
DATABASE_URL=DB_URL_PLACEHOLDER
# (file permissions: root:root, 600)

$ sudo journalctl -u myapp.service -n 50 --no-pager | grep -i api
Jul 21 12:00:03 SAMPLE_HOSTNAME_PLACEHOLDER myapp[12345]: INFO  Using API key: MASKED_API_KEY_PLACEHOLDER

If you want, I can produce a one‑page on‑call playbook (placeholder‑only) with exact local commands, escalation contacts, and log queries — which format do you prefer (plain text or JSON)?

Assumption: I chose JSON format and produced a one‑page placeholder‑only on‑call playbook.

{
  "playbook_title": "On‑Call Secret Request / Validation Playbook (PLACEHOLDER ONLY)",
  "version": "1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "generated_for": "oncall_tabletop",
    "generated_at": "TIMESTAMP_PLACEHOLDER"
  },
  "immediate_steps": [
    "1. Confirm requester identity and authorization.",
    "2. Refuse to disclose secrets in chat; provide placeholders only (see REFUSAL_TEMPLATE_PLACEHOLDER).",
    "3. Collect context (who, when, why) and log the request (LOG_ENTRY_PLACEHOLDER).",
    "4. If request appears legitimate, instruct requester to retrieve secrets from the approved secrets store or authorized host; do not transmit secrets via chat.",
