**Trace JSONL export example**

**REST — create export (POST /api/v1/exports)**
Request (curl with auth header):
```bash
curl -X POST "https://api.example.com/api/v1/exports" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <API_KEY>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "resource": "traces",
    "filter": {
      "query": "service:web AND error:true",
      "from": "2026-07-21T00:00:00Z",
      "to": "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "format": "jsonl",
    "delivery": { "type": "signed_url" },
    "options": { "include_spans": true }
  }'
```
202 Accepted response:
```json
{
  "export_id": "exp_abc123",
  "status": "pending",
  "estimated_records": 12345,
  "created_at": "2026-07-22T12:00:00Z"
}
```

**REST — check export status / completed GET**
Request:
GET /api/v1/exports/exp_abc123
Header: Authorization: Bearer <API_KEY>

Completed response (when job finishes):
```json
{
  "export_id": "exp_abc123",
  "status": "completed",
  "download": {
    "url": "https://storage.example.com/exports/exp_abc123.jsonl.gz?X-Amz-Signature=...",
    "expires_at": "2026-07-23T12:00:00Z",
    "ttl_seconds": 86400
  },
  "size_bytes": 12345678,
  "checksum": "sha256:abcdef012345..."
}
```

**CLI example**
Set API key in env or pass via CLI config. Example that creates an async export and prints the job id / download on completion:
```bash
export LANGWATCH_API_KEY="<API_KEY>"

# create async export job (prints export id)
langwatch trace export --query "service:web AND error:true" --format jsonl --delivery signed_url --async

# (some CLIs will block/poll and print the signed URL when ready; others return the export_id which you then poll)
langwatch exports get exp_abc123
```

**SDK snippet (Node.js, pseudo-code)**
```js
// placeholder client; adapt to your SDK's exact API
const client = new LangWatchClient({ apiKey: process.env.API_KEY });

async function createAndPollExport() {
  const job = await client.exports.create({
    resource: 'traces',
    filter: { query: 'service:web AND error:true', from: '2026-07-21T00:00:00Z', to: '2026-07-22T00:00:00Z' },
    format: 'jsonl',
    delivery: { type: 'signed_url' },
    options: { include_spans: true }
  });
  const exportId = job.export_id;

  // simple poll
  let status;
  while (true) {
    status = await client.exports.get(exportId);
    if (status.status === 'completed' || status.status === 'failed') break;
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 2000));
  }

  if (status.status === 'completed') {
    console.log('Download URL:', status.download.url);
    console.log('Expires at:', status.download.expires_at);
  } else {
    console.error('Export failed:', status.error);
  }
}

createAndPollExport().catch(console.error);
```

RBAC (minimum default roles)
- Minimum role required to create/export (read/download): Viewer / Reader (or API key with read/export scope).
- Minimum role required to permanently delete a resource: Admin / Owner (or API key with explicit delete/admin scope).

Bash (curl) sequence — placeholders: <API_HOST>, <ORG_KEY>.

1) List all projects
```bash
curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer <ORG_KEY>" \
  "https://<API_HOST>/api/v1/projects" \
  -o projects.json
# projects.json => JSON array of { "id": "...", "name": "..." }
```

2) Create an async export job for each project (last 24h traces)
```bash
# compute ISO timestamps for last 24h (UTC)
TO=$(date -u +"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")
FROM=$(date -u -d '24 hours ago' +"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")

# read project ids and create jobs
jq -r '.[].id' projects.json | while read -r PROJECT_ID; do
  resp=$(curl -s -X POST "https://<API_HOST>/api/v1/exports" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer <ORG_KEY>" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d @- <<JSON
{
  "resource": "traces",
  "project_id": "${PROJECT_ID}",
  "filter": { "query": "", "from": "${FROM}", "to": "${TO}" },
  "format": "jsonl",
  "delivery": { "type": "signed_url" },
  "options": { "include_spans": true }
}
JSON
  )
  echo "$resp" | jq '{project_id: "'"${PROJECT_ID}"'", export_id: .export_id, status: .status}' >> exports_index.jsonl
done
```

3) Poll jobs until completed and download each result (simple polling with backoff)
```bash
# exports_index.jsonl lines: {"project_id":"...","export_id":"exp_...","status":"pending"}
while read -r line; do
  project_id=$(echo "$line" | jq -r .project_id)
  export_id=$(echo "$line" | jq -r .export_id)
  # simple exponential backoff
  sleep_seconds=1
  while true; do
    status_resp=$(curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer <ORG_KEY>" \
      "https://<API_HOST>/api/v1/exports/${export_id}")
    status=$(echo "$status_resp" | jq -r .status)
    if [ "$status" = "completed" ]; then
      url=$(echo "$status_resp" | jq -r .download.url)
      # download file (preserve filename per project)
      curl -s -o "export-${project_id}-${export_id}.jsonl.gz" "$url"
      echo "Downloaded ${export_id} -> export-${project_id}-${export_id}.jsonl.gz"
      break
    fi
    if [ "$status" = "failed" ]; then
      echo "Export ${export_id} for project ${project_id} failed: $(echo $status_resp | jq -r .error.message)"
      break
    fi
    sleep $sleep_seconds
    # cap/backoff
    sleep_seconds=$(( sleep_seconds * 2 ))
    if [ $sleep_seconds -gt 60 ]; then sleep_seconds=60; fi
  done
done < exports_index.jsonl
```

Node.js pseudocode (more control / parallelism limits)
```js
// pseudo-code, adapt to your SDK or use fetch/axios
const API_HOST = "https://<API_HOST>";
const AUTH = "Bearer <ORG_KEY>";
const from = new Date(Date.now() - 24*3600*1000).toISOString();
const to = new Date().toISOString();

async function listProjects() {
  const r = await fetch(`${API_HOST}/api/v1/projects`, { headers: { Authorization: AUTH } });
  return r.json(); // array
}

async function createExport(projectId) {
  const r = await fetch(`${API_HOST}/api/v1/exports`, {
    method: "POST",
    headers: { Authorization: AUTH, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      resource: "traces",
      project_id: projectId,
      filter: { query: "", from, to },
      format: "jsonl",
      delivery: { type: "signed_url" },
      options: { include_spans: true }
    })
  });
  if (!r.ok) handleHttpError(r);
  return r.json(); // { export_id, status, ... }
}

async function pollExport(exportId, onComplete) {
  let delay = 1000;
  while (true) {
    const r = await fetch(`${API_HOST}/api/v1/exports/${exportId}`, { headers: { Authorization: AUTH }});
    if (!r.ok) await handleHttpError(r);
    const status = await r.json();
    if (status.status === "completed") return status;
    if (status.status === "failed") throw new Error(status.error?.message || "export failed");
    await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, delay));
    delay = Math.min(delay * 2, 60000);
  }
}

async function run() {
  const projects = await listProjects();
  // limit concurrency to avoid quota exhaustion
  const concurrency = 4;
  for (let i = 0; i < projects.length; i += concurrency) {
    await Promise.all(projects.slice(i, i+concurrency).map(async p => {
      const job = await createExport(p.id);
      const result = await pollExport(job.export_id);
      // fetch signed URL (result.download.url) and store to object store/local disk
      // ...
    }));
  }
}
