Notes and quick best-practices
- dynamic: "strict" prevents accidental ingestion of unplanned fields (good for audit indices).  
- Use nested for encoded_payloads so each encoding/entropy pair stays correlated.  
- Keep raw_message out of the index (store only raw_message_hash) unless policy explicitly permits; if you must store it, place it in a separate restricted index.  
- Apply RBAC: only the ingestion service account should have write privileges; separate read privileges for analysts.  
- Test mapping on a staging index first, then reindex into production if validated.

